# resources_mapper_texture_records: Type 11 records and validateIOSurfaceDescriptor's refusals over a one-plane surface, each its own object listed in its own exec: a short record and a short header; an unknown commandType (the surface is released); short 12, 47 and 57 operations; memoryless 12 ("Invalid storage mode (3)") and 47 descriptors; a nonzero plane ("Non zero plane in non-planar IOSurface"); a descriptor wider than the surface's rows; rows not aligned to iosurfaceTextureAlignmentBytes (surface 3, rows of 260 bytes) for a shader-read texture and for a read-write one (the read-only alignment is used only when usage & 7 is ShaderRead); taller than the surface, or an array of two slices; two mip levels; a 3D texture of depth 2; a texture buffer ("must be of type MTLTextureType2D, linear MTLTextureType2DArray or MTLTextureTypeTextureBuffer", though the check refuses exactly TextureBuffer); 47 and 57 descriptors wider than the rows. Then the good ones.
